@candidates
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
for (var id of PolishGovernment.CANDIDATE_ORDER) {
    var candidate = PolishGovernment.CANDIDATES[id];
    Q['pl_cand_' + id + '_reason'] = PolishGovernment.draftChoiceStatus(Q, 'candidate', id).reason;
    Q['pl_cand_' + id + '_note'] = (candidate.party ? PolishGovernment.ACTOR_PROFILES[candidate.party].name + ' leader' :
        'Non-party expert, programme: ' + PolishGovernment.describeProgramme(candidate.programme)) +
        (PolishGovernment.inWindow(id, Q.time) ? '. Candidate of the current period: a small advantage when the head of state compares feasible offers.' : '.');
}
Q.pl_cand_pilsudski_reason = PolishGovernment.draftChoiceStatus(Q, 'candidate', 'pilsudski').reason;
Q.pl_cand_pilsudski_note = 'Premiership agreed with Piłsudski (16.7): the programme of a legal cabinet, the usual parliamentary responsibility. The relief of pressure comes after his real appointment; this formation costs no second action.';
!}

= Choose the prime minister

A party leader needs his party in the cabinet. A non-party expert governs with the portfolios given to experts and with the support that parties sign.

- @cand_daszynski
- @cand_thugutt
- @cand_witos
- @cand_sliwinski
- @cand_nowak
- @cand_sikorski
- @cand_ponikowski
- @cand_grabski
- @cand_skrzynski
- @cand_pilsudski
- @back

